  "id": "COMPOUND:737 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between isoflurane and Macrostomia, mediated through the coiled-coil domain containing 33 (CCD33) protein. Isoflurane, a commonly used anesthetic, is shown to affect CCD33, which in turn is implicated in multiple conditions, including Hypophosphatemic rickets, Melanoma-Pancreatic cancer syndrome, and Glaucoma 1, open angle, O. These conditions are all linked to CCD33 through a causal pathway, and CCD33 is directly associated with Macrostomia. The shared involvement of CCD33 in multiple pathologies indicates a possible mechanistic link, where isoflurane may modulate CCD33 activity, leading to the development of Macrostomia. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, with similar causal relationships, suggesting a robust biological mechanism. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that isoflurane could influence Macrostomia through its effect on CCD33, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
